      "closure_rationale": "Actual positive constant1/4/8 instantiations and named capacity0/3 diagnostics distinguish constraints from chosen unused-variable and VLA warning-policy refusals. Runtime admission is actual C code for arbitrary positive capacities, not a nonconstant value falsely treated as a constant expression. Product representability and independent byte budget use the actual retained mp_storage_bound. Fixed masking requires a proven positive power of two; arbitrary runtime wrap derives a subtraction/conditional addition bound. Inspected N1570 diagnostics/constant-expression/array/static-assert clauses are explicitly C11 draft evidence, not published C17/C23. Actual Rust const-usize storage and rejected floating const type demonstrate bounded language restrictions. Six GCC/Clang debug/release/ASan+UBSan profiles match9836 FIFO histories/54615 transitions and11261 mathematical product cases; analytic16/32/64 models remain labeled. Eight compiled normal semantic controls include actual original overflow/budget defects; four learner anchors compile and reject. Actual no-libc i386 ELF32 final-links without undefined/NEEDED dependencies and executes under QEMU Linux-user, including both original arithmetic controls rejected. Missing hosted32bit headers/libraries remains a distinct availability gap. Compile-time capacities1/4/8 and volatile runtime capacities1through17 preserve full/empty/initialization failure and FIFO. Runtime3 uses conditional wrapping instead of a mask; reduced byte budget rejects without publication. Actual O0/O3 object/disassembly and clean/unchanged builds accompany seven equal100000round samples/checksum600000, including runtime initialization and backing storage in the comparison. All13 dimensions retain ABI, pointer-lifetime and nonconcurrency boundaries. Bounded author support only."
